      <author_list>Barnouin, O.; Daly, T.; Ernst, C.; Espiritu, R.; Waller, D.</author_list>
      <publication_year>2023</publication_year>
      <description>The shape of 65803 Didymos is obtained using stereophotoclinometry where stereo techniques with photoclinometry
        is used to derive the tilt of an asteroid’s  surface from DRACO images.
        The model resolution is approximately 9.309m between vertices. The model has the format
        v x1 y1 z1
        v x2 y2 z2
        v x3 y3 z3
        (etc.)
        f i1 j1 k1
        f i2 j2 k2
        (etc.)
        where the letter 'v' denotes a vertex and the letter 'f' denotes a triangular facet.
        A comment with # is provided at the beginning of the file providing
        More details about the shape. See DART Shape Model SIS for more
        details.
      </description>
    </Citation_Information>
